Movie Dataset Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) - Alex The Analyst Portfolio Project 4
This repository contains an exploratory data analysis (EDA) of a movie dataset. The project aims to uncover patterns and relationships between various movie attributes, focusing on factors that influence financial success and critical reception. This notebook is the fourth project in the portfolio project series by Alex The Analyst.

Project Objective
The primary goal of this project is to analyze the "movies.csv" dataset to find patterns and understand the factors influencing movie success, particularly focusing on financial performance (gross earnings) and critical reception (score/rating).

Data Source
The dataset used in this analysis is "movies.csv", which was downloaded from Kaggle.

Analysis Steps
The analysis in this notebook followed a structured approach:

Data Loading and Initial Understanding: Loaded the dataset, inspected data types, identified missing values, and obtained basic statistics.
Data Cleaning: Handled missing values by dropping rows in key columns and checked for duplicates.
Data Type Conversion: Converted relevant numerical columns to integer types.
Year Consistency Check: Examined and handled inconsistencies between the 'year' and 'released' date columns.
Correlation Analysis: Explored relationships between numerical features using scatter plots, regression plots, and correlation matrices (Pearson, Kendall, Spearman).
Handling Categorical Data: Converted categorical columns to numerical representations using the .cat.codes method for further analysis.
Expanded Correlation Analysis: Analyzed the correlation matrix including numerized categorical features.
Deepened Categorical Analysis (Genre and Company): Visualized and analyzed the distribution of gross earnings and scores by genre and company using box plots and bar charts of median values.
Visualizing Numerical Feature Distributions: Created histograms and box plots to understand the distribution of key numerical features.
Analyzing Trends Over Time (Optional): Explored median trends of key metrics over the years.
Interpretation and Narrative: Added detailed markdown cells to interpret findings and create a clear narrative.

Key Findings
Budget strongly correlates with gross
Votes correlate with gross
Genres and big studios skew revenue higher
Scores have a weaker link to revenue

Skills Demonstrated
Data Loading and Inspection (pandas)
Data Cleaning and Handling Missing Values
Data Type Conversion
Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Correlation Analysis (Pearson, Kendall, Spearman)
Data Visualization (matplotlib, seaborn)
Handling Categorical Data
Interpreting Statistical Measures
Data Grouping and Aggregation

How to Run the Notebook
Clone this repository.
Ensure you have Python and the necessary libraries installed (pandas, numpy, seaborn, matplotlib).
Place the movies.csv file in the correct directory (or update the file path in the notebook).
Open and run the Jupyter Notebook or Google Colab notebook.
